From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Radoslav Furnadzhiev <dinozavyrtrex@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: rockchip: grf: rk3588: disable auto jtag/sdmmc switching

RK3588 resets with SYS_GRF_SOC_CON6 bit 14 (force_jtag) set. If the
SDMMC controller sees no card detect, the SDMMC data pins switch to JTAG.
An SDIO device without card detect then fails in 4-bit and UHS modes.
Clear the bit at boot, as for RK3288 and RK3399.
---
--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/grf.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/grf.c
@@ -242,9 +242,11 @@
 	.num_values = ARRAY_SIZE(rk3566_defaults),
 };
 
+#define RK3588_SYS_GRF_SOC_CON6		0x0318
 #define RK3588_SYS_GRF_SOC_CON7		0x031c
 
 static const struct rockchip_grf_value rk3588_sys_grf_defaults[] __initconst = {
+	{ "jtag switching", RK3588_SYS_GRF_SOC_CON6, HIWORD_UPDATE(0, 1, 14) },
 	{ "Connect EDP hpd to IO", RK3588_SYS_GRF_SOC_CON7, HIWORD_UPDATE(0x3, 0x3, 14) },
 };
 
